---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/sequenzy-vs-yotpo-email-sms";
const title = "Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS for Shopify: 2026 Decision Guide";
const desc = "Replace a retired sender while retaining reviews. A scoped Shopify workflow comparison with current product evidence and proposed acceptance checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I newly choose Yotpo Email & SMS in 2026?",
    "answer": "Yotpo announced full deprecation for December 31, 2025. Treat this as a replacement decision and verify any account-specific access with Yotpo."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Sequenzy a Yotpo-named migration partner?",
    "answer": "The cited Yotpo announcement names Attentive and Omnisend. Evaluate Sequenzy separately rather than implying endorsement."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Inventory reviews and loyalty separately from the retired sender. Confirm the retained services and which app owns each customer message."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will review and loyalty fields sync to Sequenzy automatically?",
    "answer": "Do not assume so. Confirm a supported bridge, field identity and update behavior for each required workflow."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does replacing email restore SMS?",
    "answer": "No. Verify destination coverage, sender registration, permission records and opt-out handling independently. Sequenzy advertises an optional US/Canada add-on."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if my old exports are unavailable?",
    "answer": "Ask the account owner and support about retrieval and use retained merchant records where appropriate. Mark missing consent and history explicitly rather than reconstructing them from assumptions."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Shopify decision guide</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">This is now a replacement-planning page. Yotpo announced full deprecation of Email and SMS for December 31, 2025. A Shopify merchant reading this in 2026 should not compare a new Yotpo Email subscription against Sequenzy as though both were current choices. Reviews and Loyalty responsibilities still need a separate inventory.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Current status changes the decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo announced the Email/SMS sunset and named Attentive and Omnisend as migration partners. That announcement establishes the retirement plan; it is not evidence of a current extension for a particular account or guaranteed export access. Ask the account owner or support what remains retrievable. Sequenzy is another email candidate to evaluate, not a named partner in that announcement.</p>
      <h2>Recover the operating record first</h2>
      <p>Inventory whatever exports and configuration records remain: subscribed contacts, channel-specific permission evidence, suppressions, templates, active segments, flow diagrams and reporting definitions. Mark unavailable records explicitly. Do not rebuild a marketing list from orders alone or infer SMS consent from a phone number. If export access has ended, use retained merchant records and support assistance to establish what can safely be restored.</p>
      <h2>Reviews are not the email sender</h2>
      <p>Separate review collection, onsite display, loyalty updates and promotional messages in an ownership table. For each, record the responsible app, trigger and recipient rule. Keeping Yotpo Reviews does not require assuming Yotpo Email still operates. Likewise, choosing Sequenzy does not establish that review text, star ratings, loyalty points or tier-change events arrive in its customer records.</p>
      <h2>Proposed trial: review request and care guide</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical skincare store, keep the review request with the designated review service and rebuild a product care guide in the candidate email sender. Use an order with two products and delayed delivery. Check whether the guide relies on order, fulfillment or delivery data, and whether review requests collide with it. This is a proposed operating test, not a reported brand result. Agree timing from the actual product and service experience rather than a universal post-purchase delay.</p>
      <h2>Prove review data before personalizing</h2>
      <p>If a follow-up branches on whether a shopper has reviewed a specific product, require product and review identity in the event or data model. A permanent reviewer tag only says something happened at some time; it may not answer whether this order has a review. Define who maintains the bridge and how edits or deletions propagate. If no supported route exists, use non-review-dependent copy rather than silently treating missing data as a negative review state.</p>
      <h2>Replace SMS independently when necessary</h2>
      <p>Sequenzy advertises optional US/Canada SMS, so it should not be dismissed as email-only. Still compare sender registration, recipient destinations, consent transfer and opt-out handling with the requirements of the old program. A replacement email flow does not restore a retired text number or transfer its permission history. Plan a supported SMS destination separately if the proposed email candidate cannot meet those needs.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild segments with explicit limits</h2>
      <p>Historical revenue and audience membership may not reproduce when the destination uses different event history or attribution windows. Save the old definition and document the new one. Start with explainable criteria, such as an actual purchase history field confirmed in the account, rather than assuming every Yotpo-derived segment can be imported as live logic. Keep snapshot lists labeled as snapshots and establish how membership will be refreshed.</p>
      <h2>Budget and cutover without suite assumptions</h2>
      <p>Compare the replacement sender, SMS service if needed, retained review/loyalty subscriptions and bridge maintenance. The discontinued bundle is not a current price benchmark. Before enabling new recovery or post-purchase entry points, check every surviving app for equivalent messages. Preserve available exports and a record of destination field mappings. Choose Sequenzy when its demonstrated email workflow fits; choose another candidate when channel or ecosystem requirements remain unmet.</p>
      <h2>Sources and evaluation limits</h2>
      <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. These are documented capabilities and proposed decision checks, not firsthand product tests or measured merchant results. Account eligibility, payloads and current quotes need confirmation before activation.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo sunset and named partners</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/about">Sequenzy scope</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/supplements">Email apps for supplement stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
